  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3cc91986",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 8. Scaling Up: Multi-Category Parallel Ingestion\n",
    "\n",
    "So far, we have tested our pipeline on a single category (`Appliances`). To build a robust, general-purpose valuation model, we need diversity across the e-commerce spectrum.\n",
    "\n",
    "### ⚡ The Multiprocessing Architecture (`pricer.loaders.ItemLoader`)\n",
    "Sequential parsing of millions of raw records in Python would take hours due to the Global Interpreter Lock (GIL). \n",
    "[`ItemLoader`](file:///C:/Amit/work/code/AI/llm_engineering/myself/Week6/pricer/loaders.py) solves this by:\n",
    "1. Dividing the dataset into batches of 1,000 records (`CHUNK_SIZE = 1000`).\n",
    "2. Spawning a `ProcessPoolExecutor` utilizing `cpu_count - 1` CPU cores.\n",
    "3. Distributing parsing and regex scrubbing across all cores in parallel, cutting ingestion time by 80–90%.\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's test `ItemLoader` on Appliances to verify its speed:\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9e60de0f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pricer.loaders import ItemLoader\n",
    "loader = ItemLoader(\"Appliances\")\n",
    "items = loader.load()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2764201a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 📦 Ingesting 8 Diverse Product Categories\n",
    "\n",
    "We now ingest 8 major e-commerce categories to ensure rich product diversity:\n",
    "1. **Automotive**: Car parts, accessories, maintenance tools.\n",
    "2. **Electronics**: Gadgets, audio equipment, cables, consumer tech.\n",
    "3. **Office Products**: Stationery, furniture, organizational supplies.\n",
    "4. **Tools & Home Improvement**: Power tools, hardware, fixtures.\n",
    "5. **Cell Phones & Accessories**: Cases, chargers, mounts, phones.\n",
    "6. **Toys & Games**: Board games, outdoor toys, action figures.\n",
    "7. **Appliances**: Kitchen appliances, vacuums, parts.\n",
    "8. **Musical Instruments**: Guitars, keyboards, studio audio gear.\n",
    "\n",
    "> ⚠️ **Resource Warning & CPU Load**:\n",
    "> Ingesting and parsing all 8 categories processes almost **3 million raw records**. \n",
    "> - **Execution Time**: Takes ~10–15 minutes if cached, but can take up to an hour on a fresh run as datasets are downloaded from Hugging Face.\n",
    "> - **Hardware Stress**: It will heavily utilize your CPU across all available cores.\n",
    "> - **Optional**: Ed Donner has already run this and published the resulting dataset to Hugging Face (`ed-donner/items_raw_full` and `ed-donner/items_raw_lite`). You do not have to run this cell if you prefer to use the pre-curated version!\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4db93832",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "dataset_names = [\n",
    "    \"Automotive\",\n",
    "    \"Electronics\",\n",
    "    \"Office_Products\",\n",
    "    \"Tools_and_Home_Improvement\",\n",
    "    \"Cell_Phones_and_Accessories\",\n",
    "    \"Toys_and_Games\",\n",
    "    \"Appliances\",\n",
    "    \"Musical_Instruments\",\n",
    "]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3065e568",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Let's execute the multi-category loading loop:\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f6382c4a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "items = []\n",
    "for dataset_name in dataset_names:\n",
    "    loader = ItemLoader(dataset_name)\n",
    "    items.extend(loader.load())"
   ]
  },
