   "source": [
    "### 11. Diagnosing the Two Major Flaws\n",
    "\n",
    "Examining our 2.887 million items reveals **two critical flaws** that would compromise model training:\n",
    "1. **Severe Category Imbalance**: As the bar chart demonstrates, **Automotive** alone accounts for nearly **1 million items**! **Tools & Home Improvement** is second. Categories like **Musical Instruments** and **Appliances** are dwarfed.\n",
    "2. **Severe Price Skew**: The overwhelming majority of products cost under $40.\n",
    "\n",
    "> ⚠️ **The Consequence**: If trained on this raw data, the model will essentially become a *car parts pricer for cheap items*, failing when asked to value an expensive musical instrument or electronic device!\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6e2955c4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "category_counts = Counter([item.category for item in items])\n",
    "\n",
    "categories = category_counts.keys()\n",
    "counts = [category_counts[category] for category in categories]\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(15, 6))\n",
    "plt.bar(categories, counts, color=\"goldenrod\")\n",
    "plt.title('How many in each category')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Categories')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Count')\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=30, ha='right')\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, v in enumerate(counts):\n",
    "    plt.text(i, v, f\"{v:,}\", ha='center', va='bottom')\n",
