    "> 💡 **Finding on Weight vs. Price**:\n",
    "> 1. **The Weight = 0 Cluster**: You will notice a noticeable vertical stripe of items at `Weight = 0` across all price ranges. In web scrapes, many product listings fail to list weight in their technical specs, or format it in ways that default to 0.\n",
    "> 2. **Positive Correlation for Weighed Goods**: For products with recorded weights, there is a clear upward slope—heavy appliances and large power tools naturally command higher prices.\n",
    "> 3. **The Semantic Gap**: However, high-ticket lightweight goods (e.g. an $800 smartphone weighing 0.4 lbs vs. a $40 set of 50 lb barbell weights) prove that physical attributes alone cannot predict price. Accurate pricing demands **deep semantic understanding** of brands, specifications, and materials.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "## 16. Dataset Partitioning & Pushing to Hugging Face Hub\n",
    "\n",
    "We now split our curated 820,000 items into standard machine learning partitions:\n",
    "- **`train`**: 800,000 items (for large-scale fine-tuning)\n",
    "- **`validation`**: 10,000 items (for hyperparameter tuning and early stopping)\n",
    "- **`test`**: 10,000 items (held-out gold standard for benchmark evaluations)\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🚀 The \"Full\" vs. \"Lite\" Datasets\n",
    "Throughout the course, we maintain two parallel datasets:\n",
    "1. **`items_raw_full`**: The heavyweight dataset containing all **820,000 items** (800k train, 10k val, 10k test).\n",
    "2. **`items_raw_lite`**: A streamlined dataset of **22,000 items** (20,000 train, 1,000 val, 1,000 test) for fast iteration, quick debugging, and training on free Colab tiers without waiting days for compute.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🌐 Public vs. Private on Hugging Face Hub\n",
    "- By default, datasets created via the Hugging Face API are private.\n",
    "- Ed Donner's versions (`ed-donner/items_raw_full` and `ed-donner/items_raw_lite`) are made **public**, so you can easily load them tomorrow without having to spend hours running the local ingestion loop!\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "01e3ee1c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "username = \"ed-donner\"\n",
    "full = f\"{username}/items_raw_full\"\n",
    "lite = f\"{username}/items_raw_lite\"\n",
    "\n",
    "train = sample[:800_000]\n",
    "val = sample[800_000:810_000]\n",
    "test = sample[810_000:]\n",
    "\n",
    "Item.push_to_hub(full, train, val, test)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_lite = train[:20_000]\n",
    "val_lite = val[:1_000]\n",
    "test_lite = test[:1_000]\n",
    "\n",
    "Item.push_to_hub(lite, train_lite, val_lite, test_lite)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e08b2433",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 17. Summary & Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "### ✅ What We Accomplished in Day 1:\n",
    "1. **Raw Ingestion & Schema Exploration**: Explored raw Amazon metadata from McAuley Lab and solved the missing-price phenomenon.\n",
    "2. **Outlier Discovery**: Identified commercial extremes like the $21,000 TurboChef microwave convection oven and bounded prices to $1,000.\n",
    "3. **Data Quality & Parsing Pipeline**: Standardized prices ($0.50–$999.49), filtered short descriptions (<600 chars), stripped boilerplate metadata & non-semantic ASIN/regex codes, and normalized diverse weight units into pounds.\n",
    "4. **High-Throughput Multiprocessing**: Utilized `ItemLoader` and `ProcessPoolExecutor` across `cpu_count - 1` cores to ingest ~3 million raw records across 8 product categories.\n",
    "5. **Deduplication**: Eliminated duplicate titles and repeated marketing copy to prevent test leakage and avoid the **False Validation Trap**.\n",
    "6. **Stratified Resampling**: Applied quadratic price weighting ($w = p^2$) and a 95% Automotive penalty to lift the average price from $59 to $140 and rebalance category shares.\n",
    "7. **Feature Correlation Analysis**: Discovered that neither text length nor weight alone can predict price, proving the necessity of semantic LLM models.\n",
    "8. **Hub Publication**: Partitioned into Train/Val/Test (Full 820k and Lite 22k) splits and published to Hugging Face Hub.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "### 🚀 Coming Up in Day 2: Advanced LLM Engineering\n",
    "Tomorrow we take this curated dataset and begin preparing it for model training:\n",
    "1. **The 5-Step Strategy**: A structured framework for selecting, training, and applying LLMs in production.\n",
    "2. **Dataset Pre-processing with LLMs**: Using LLMs to summarize, cleanse, and structure product features into clean training prompts.\n",
    "3. **Batch Mode API Calls**: Moving beyond synchronous request-response to asynchronous bulk batch inference—an advanced LLM engineering practice that slashes costs and handles high-throughput pipelines.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
